A||N||10||rockcrawl||My new side scoops are ready !!!||||7||
Z||000000||rockcrawl||09-12-2000||08:21 PM||||OK, Here they are. I painted a set and installed them on my Yellow 3.8 GT to give you guys an idea how they look on the car.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ss1.jpg">  <P> The paint is not an exact match, and the car was dripping wet. I gave up on the double sided tape mounting method, although I still think it would work for someone who doesn't want to drill holes. The scoops have a full 1/2" mounting flange on the inside, and 4 threaded steel inserts are glassed in during lay-up. They have a smooth white gelcoat finish that is ready for paint. They are molded directly from a set of OEM Fiero quarter panels to ensure the perfect contour. The mesh screen will be included and it is the same type of material that you see in the defrost vents on the dash. I was able to mount mine without removing the quarter panels. I removed some of the screws from the inner fender and reached in behind. I will supply the screws and a template for drilling the holes. <BR> The wonderful township I live in has finally approved my lot subdivision (after a whole year) which means I can start building my new house. This leaves me with no extra time to work on making these scoops. I have a few pairs completed and ready to ship. I'll be listing them on Ebay to give everyone a shot a getting them. I know this may upset a few people, but it's what I have to do. Ok, here are the rest of the pics:<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ss2.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ss3.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ss4.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ss5.jpg">  <P>I think they would look even better if the insides of the scoops and the area covered by the scoops were painted black.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<p>[This message has been edited by rockcrawl (edited 09-12-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000001||Sage||09-12-2000||09:39 PM||||Nice job Rock!  They look very good on your car, and the workmanship and care that went into making them shows.<P>Keep up the good work, and have a good one!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Sage (edited 09-12-2000).]||||reg||1
